{"id": "EUVD-2026-67487", "enisaUuid": "060cf93c-f925-3cf4-8627-ff8ac3deefa9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nACPI: processor_idle: Mark LPI enter functions as __cpuidle\n\nWhen function tracing or Kprobes is enabled, entering an ACPI Low\nPower Idle (LPI) state triggers the following RCU splat:\n\n  RCU not on for: acpi_idle_lpi_enter+0x4/0xd8\n  WARNING: CPU: 8 PID: 0 at include/linux/trace_recursion.h:162 function_trace_call+0x1e8/0x228\n\nThe acpi_idle_lpi_enter() function is invoked within the cpuidle\npath after RCU has already been disabled for the current local CPU.\nConsequently, ftrace's function_trace_call() expects RCU to be\nactively watching before recording trace data, emitting a warning\nif it is not.\n\nFix this by annotating acpi_idle_lpi_enter(), the generic __weak\nstub, and the RISC-V implementation of acpi_processor_ffh_lpi_enter()\nwith __cpuidle. This moves these functions into the '.cpuidle.text'\nsection, implicitly disabling ftrace instrumentation (notrace) along\nthis sensitive path and preventing trace-induced RCU warnings during\nidle entry.", "datePublished": "2026-08-28T06:48:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:46:33", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c17fe25dcb55ab94f6aa2930b7504ea666d5fcc2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/10f675902a5fc88ccfe34bb8aa37de50806b03b1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5b6165d7ec38477e8cfa41bfa464959957953822", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8bbe4dd7964552f74c271c3a8d95a4331a8ab5f9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/956ca5d72c76504824c8eb601879da9476973e15"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vvhc-p9vw-ph6p", "CVE-2026-80611"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "13c14b44-8ecf-3151-bc02-58d0e4ce8580", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "205c489d-7612-3c67-9ee6-df250a5ac2b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "2dc5fe81-e219-35d6-9624-c0bc3b612fe9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a36a7fecfe6071732075ad5aa31196adce13181b <c17fe25dcb55ab94f6aa2930b7504ea666d5fcc2"}, {"id": "3e054067-0bb6-33c9-baed-fb45214bd629", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a36a7fecfe6071732075ad5aa31196adce13181b <8bbe4dd7964552f74c271c3a8d95a4331a8ab5f9"}, {"id": "41649c4f-ec5a-329c-9a74-f355ed168024", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "61be34e3-9019-34e3-8e70-f40c92abbf53", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "68393603-666f-3b02-8a27-4a24c433b676", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a36a7fecfe6071732075ad5aa31196adce13181b <956ca5d72c76504824c8eb601879da9476973e15"}, {"id": "68d5a4ce-f21b-3154-a71f-a1c5b7b10d79", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a36a7fecfe6071732075ad5aa31196adce13181b <10f675902a5fc88ccfe34bb8aa37de50806b03b1"}, {"id": "6dc16326-0b02-3d3c-8658-b65eede62ab9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "d786f223-fffd-3b55-9547-381de22037d1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a36a7fecfe6071732075ad5aa31196adce13181b <5b6165d7ec38477e8cfa41bfa464959957953822"}, {"id": "d98d7e33-78ae-3311-9cf5-8516b26200dd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "fa2c4055-fc9d-3fa3-abef-1b396fbcdea1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b350e8a9-f8c2-36ab-973a-4bb434ad0128", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}